title a native video codec that encodes a 4x4 pixel buffer to a 4x4 pixel buffer
witness a claim in `diag gfx` that a video frame of size 4x4 is encoded and decoded correctly, which fails today because the `encode` and `decode` functions are not implemented
why this is the next thing and not a later one because the video codec must be implemented in a file that can be checked without hardware, and this is the first step toward a functional video codec in the kernel
